#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/managing_hosts.rst:80
msgid ""
"Adding a 4th host to a 3-node cluster increases the majority requirement "
"from 2 to 3 without improving failure tolerance. Consider adding hosts in"
" pairs (3→5, 5→7) for optimal availability."
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/managing_hosts.rst:83
msgid "Verification After Adding"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/managing_hosts.rst:85
msgid "After the new host is provisioned:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/managing_hosts.rst:87
msgid ""
"Navigate to ``Infrastructure > Clusters > [Cluster] > Summary > Quorum`` "
"panel"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/managing_hosts.rst:88
msgid "Confirm the total node count has increased"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/managing_hosts.rst:89
msgid "Confirm the new host shows as ONLINE"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/managing_hosts.rst:90
msgid "On the new host, verify Corosync membership:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/managing_hosts.rst:92
msgid "corosync-quorumtool -l"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/managing_hosts.rst:96
msgid "Verify DLM sees all members:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/managing_hosts.rst:98
msgid "dlm_tool status -v"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/managing_hosts.rst:102
msgid ""
"Compare physical-interface inventory with ``sudo hvmcli interfaces list "
"--filter ethernet``. If an interface was added to the host after "
"enrollment, follow the Netplan and UI refresh procedure in :ref:`hvm-"
"host-prep` before assigning it to a Virtual Switch."
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/managing_hosts.rst:105
msgid "Removing a Host from an Existing Cluster"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/managing_hosts.rst:107
msgid ""
"Hosts can be removed from an HVM cluster when decommissioning hardware, "
"reducing cluster size, or replacing failed nodes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/managing_hosts.rst:109
msgid "Warning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/managing_hosts.rst:109
msgid ""
"Removing a host reduces the cluster's failure tolerance. Ensure the "
"remaining cluster size still meets your availability requirements before "
"proceeding."
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/managing_hosts.rst:114
msgid "Before removing a host:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/managing_hosts.rst:116
msgid ""
"Confirm the cluster layout and ensure the resulting cluster will still "
"have quorum (at minimum 3 nodes for a single-site cluster)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/managing_hosts.rst:117
msgid ""
"Confirm the Quorum panel reports ACHIEVED, all surviving hosts are "
"reachable, lockspaces are healthy, and shared datastores are mounted with"
" healthy paths"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/managing_hosts.rst:118
msgid ""
"Evacuate all VMs from the host using maintenance mode (see "
":doc:`host_maintenance`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/managing_hosts.rst:119
msgid "Verify no VMs are pinned to the host that cannot be moved"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/managing_hosts.rst:120
msgid ""
"Confirm no local or raw-device VM remains on the host and that remaining "
"hosts have the required VM networks and storage access"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/managing_hosts.rst:125
msgid ""
"Place the host in maintenance mode to evacuate VMs (see "
":doc:`host_maintenance`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/managing_hosts.rst:126
msgid "Navigate to ``Infrastructure > Clusters > [Cluster] > Hosts``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/managing_hosts.rst:127
msgid "Select the host to remove"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/managing_hosts.rst:128
msgid "Click :guilabel:`Remove`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/managing_hosts.rst:129
msgid "Confirm the removal"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/managing_hosts.rst:130
msgid ""
"Wait for the removal operation to finish; do not manually edit Corosync "
"or Agent quorum files"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/managing_hosts.rst:135
msgid ""
"When a host is removed from a layout 1.3 or 2.0 cluster, |morpheus| "
"performs the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/managing_hosts.rst:137
msgid ""
"**GFS2 unmount** — All HPE Clustered Datastores (GFS2 filesystems) are "
"unmounted on the departing host"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/managing_hosts.rst:139
msgid ""
"**Cluster services stop** — DLM and Corosync are stopped and disabled on "
"the departing host"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/managing_hosts.rst:141
msgid ""
"**Corosync configuration update** — The departing host's node block is "
"removed from ``corosync.conf`` on all remaining hosts. The configuration "
"is archived (backed up to ``/etc/corosync/archive/``), ``config_version``"
" is incremented, and ``corosync-cfgtool -R`` reloads the configuration "
"live on each remaining host"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/managing_hosts.rst:143
msgid ""
"**Datastore cleanup** — Each datastore's location reference to the "
"removed host is cleaned up"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/managing_hosts.rst:145
msgid ""
"**Quorum list update** — Updated ``quorumInfo`` is sent to all remaining "
"agents. The departing host is removed from ``.quorum-nodes`` on all "
"cluster members"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/managing_hosts.rst:148
msgid "Quorum Impact When Removing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/managing_hosts.rst:172
msgid "2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/managing_hosts.rst:175
msgid "Important"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/managing_hosts.rst:175
msgid ""
"Never reduce a single-site cluster below 3 nodes. A 2-node cluster cannot"
" achieve quorum if either node fails, resulting in a complete cluster "
"outage."
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/managing_hosts.rst:178
msgid "Handling Offline Host Removal"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/managing_hosts.rst:180
msgid "If the host to be removed is offline (powered off or unreachable):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/managing_hosts.rst:182
msgid ""
"First confirm the host is powered off or otherwise cannot access shared "
"storage. If isolation cannot be proven, do not remove it; contact HPE "
"Support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/managing_hosts.rst:183
msgid ""
"Use the same UI :guilabel:`Remove` action. On layout 1.3 and later, "
"|morpheus| removes the node from the Corosync ring using surviving online"
" hosts and updates Agent quorum membership"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/managing_hosts.rst:184
msgid ""
"If the departing node is still active in the Corosync ring, or the "
"updated Corosync configuration cannot be written consistently to all "
"survivors, |morpheus| aborts the reload and raises an alarm rather than "
"risk partitioning the ring"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/managing_hosts.rst:185
msgid ""
"If no other hosts are online, cleanup cannot proceed and |morpheus| "
"raises an **Unable to remove host** alarm"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/managing_hosts.rst:187
msgid ""
"Do not publish or use direct host-shell removal commands as a substitute "
"for this workflow. If the UI operation raises an alarm or cannot "
"establish a safe ring departure, retain the host record and contact HPE "
"Support."
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/managing_hosts.rst:190
msgid "Post-removal Verification"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/managing_hosts.rst:192
msgid "Confirm the host no longer appears in the cluster Hosts list"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/managing_hosts.rst:193
msgid ""
"Confirm the Quorum panel reports ACHIEVED with the new member count and "
"no removed host under down, fenced, or unclean members"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/managing_hosts.rst:194
msgid ""
"Confirm Corosync and DLM list only the remaining members and lockspaces "
"are healthy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/managing_hosts.rst:195
msgid ""
"Confirm every shared datastore is mounted and healthy on every remaining "
"host"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/managing_hosts.rst:196
msgid ""
"Confirm evacuated or failed-over VMs run once, on hosts with their "
"required networks and storage"
msgstr ""

